Z||000000||Cliff Pennock||01-11-2000||07:16 PM||||20 minutes after I posted my message in the "Ok, who got armed for Y2K" thread, about how crime is getting out of hand here in Holland, somebody threw a brick through my shop's window downstairs, got in, took some equipment and took off. I was reading another message here on the forum when it happened. I ran downstairs and the guy was still in the shop climbing out of the window. I probably could have ran after him (although that wouldn't have been such a good idea - bare feet with all that glass laying around) but chose to call the police immediately instead. In hindsight, I'm glad I did, because as I tried to explain in my other message, you don't know who's carrying a gun nowadays.<P>Anyway, as it looks now there's about $2000 worth of damage. The piece of equipment he took was worth $25.<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||Richard Parnell||01-11-2000||07:20 PM||||Sounds like Holland? is getting as nuts as a lot of other places.  People around here are horrible, they seem to think that if there is something lying around and no one attached to it, it must be theirs.  From what you've said before the police around your town are not much help either.  Sorry for you loss.||||reg||9
