Z||000020||DJRice||01-12-2000||08:48 AM||||FOr those who have troubles with people letting themselves into a garage, RadioShack makes a small battery powered Passive IR motion detector that will "ding-dong" when someone passes through its field of view.  This noise could get irritating, but if you have troubles with people letting themself in, the $25 might be a good deterrent.<P>Just a thought.||||reg||1
Z||000021||stsmithgt||01-12-2000||10:55 AM||||Noise is a great deturant.  My Grandpa had a ringer on his garage door.  It worked real well.  Of course an insane gun toting attitude that's well known works well also.  The last for years I've parked my car on the street with a known crack house across the street!  With all the traffic they had, they and their hoodlum crackheads knew better than to touch my car.  Oh yeah, I guess the 120 lbs. German shepard NITRO had something to do with them staying away. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>A little late Cliff, but a dog like Nitro would have helped you.  Nitro knows what crackheads taste like.  It's just the bloody mess you have to clean up afterwards that's a pain.  The local police like him.||||reg||1
Z||000022||RFMike||01-12-2000||11:04 PM||||Ogre is right about the laminated glass.  If you go that route, contact a distributor for skylight glass.  I don't know what is available in Holland, but in the U.S., Viracon sells the glass directly to anybocy who wants it.  Also try a company called Supersky.  They make skylights, and will sell glass directly.  This glass can be had in 1/4" through 5/8" laminate (two layers with a skin between).  The 5/8" stuff is nearly bullet proof.<BR>If that doesn't do it, aim between the eyes.||||reg||1
